  "diagnosis": {
    "established": "Prepared-base build completed. The first source guest timed out before authenticated SSH READY; graceful powerdown also failed. Inner containment required force, reached zero processes and removed the owned fixture. Outer controller completion was normal but nonzero; it does not prove graceful guest shutdown.",
    "serialObservation": "The retained guest serial tail shows first-boot cloud-init completing at guest wall time01:15:12Z, finalizer cloud-init/identity/reboot, then kernel reboot at uptime12.702402s. These prior guest lines were copied into the host log at01:29:05Z. No second boot is shown; a reboot loop is not proven.",
    "workingHypothesis": "Guest-initiated WHPX reset stalls after identity initialization. An exact pinned-binary/normal-profile differential is required; no accelerator or source correction has been approved from upstream reports alone.",
    "candidateControls": "Fresh focused original-WHPX and WHPX with software interrupt-controller diagnostics are being compared. Tiny firmware-only QMP reset responses do not prove Linux reboot or authenticated READY.",
    "notAssumed": "No ACL/startup regression or identical historical hosted root cause is inferred. EzVM PR45 is not imported.",
